# Paul problem protocol

When Paul challenges a finding, reports the account/dashboard does not
match, or otherwise finds a problem with what you told him, he will ask
(explicitly or by habit) these three questions. **Answer all three every
time**, even if he only pastes a complaint without numbering them:

1. **How did this happen?** — exact root cause / mechanism.
2. **What are you doing to fix it?** — concrete in-flight or shipped fix.
3. **What are you doing so this AND ANYTHING LIKE THIS will NEVER HAPPEN AGAIN?** — class-level prevention (guard + test + automated check), not a one-off.

Do not answer with analysis alone. Ship or schedule the fix and the
prevention in the same turn when possible.

Standing Kalshi/kitchen notes: secrets are local-only; use
`run_kalshi_recon_dump.bat` for venue truth; combined dashboard P&L can
hide Kalshi losses; Yes on player A + No on player B on Kalshi is a
same-direction double, not a lock.

Prevention shipped 2026-11-01: `tools/kalshi_same_direction.py`,
send gates in `live_lock_orders`, `run_kalshi_venue_kitchen_check.bat`.
